      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-08T18:21:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Dawn Ra is awesome, especially if you can grap Omnitron or Operative with the third. &nbsp;You use Ra like you use Ambuscade's Traps, but with the pillar, Solar flare and Dawn's buff with citizen Truth protecting Ra give you some great damage.I've used Unity too, but you need better protection than Stealth Bot.If you can grab Omnitron with your first pick, then Unity Ra would be amazing for your others. &nbsp;Keep Ra in the trees, and keep him next to Champion Bot and Turret Bot. &nbsp;Then have Omnitron run enemies through the gambit of Turret Bott at 5D and Ra's Tornado or Living Pyre at even more.Still are vulnerable to origin attacks, but you can throw down some crazy damage.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You made me think of something interesting. Character Bans will have an impact on the teams chosen, but the environment can have a big impact too. I'd hazard to guess that a map comprised mostly of Insula Primalis would see more Bunker play where as a map that was more city might see some Tachyon impact. Tachyon doesn't fair well in wide open spaces and Bunker hates moving through buildings. I'd be interested to see some map shake ups in the next tourney</p>",
